{%- comment -%}
  OPTIONAL — cart-page-only "Coming soon" notice for ichillpod.com (Dawn 16.0.0).
  Only use if the Shopify-native cart/checkout wording (runbook §3-A) is not acceptable.

  HOW TO APPLY (theme editor only, no code files touched):
    Online Store -> Themes -> Customize -> template dropdown -> Cart
    -> Add section -> "Custom Liquid" -> paste this whole file into the Liquid box
    -> drag the section to the top (above "Cart items") -> Save.

  WHERE IT RENDERS: the /cart page only. Never on the product page, homepage, header,
  collections or any marketing section. Buy Now / Shop Pay / all storefront chrome untouched.

  WHEN IT RENDERS: only while the chillpod product is unavailable (inventory 0, continue
  selling off) OR the cart holds a line item whose variant is unavailable. Once inventory is
  restored the notice disappears by itself; the section can then be removed via the editor.

  Nothing here blocks checkout. The inventory hard stop (runbook §1) does that.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign coming_soon_product = all_products['chillpod']
  assign show_coming_soon = false
  if coming_soon_product != blank and coming_soon_product.available == false
    assign show_coming_soon = true
  endif
  for item in cart.items
    if item.variant.available == false
      assign show_coming_soon = true
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- if show_coming_soon -%}
  <div class="page-width">
    <div
      role="status"
      aria-live="polite"
      style="border: 0.1rem solid rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.2); padding: 1.6rem 2rem; margin: 0 0 1rem;"
    >
      <p class="h4" style="margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Coming soon — should be available within the next 30 days.</p>
      <p style="margin: 0;">iChillPod can't be ordered right now, so this cart can't be checked out yet. Nothing has been charged. Please check back soon.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
